un different things and cite different evidence. Fix: record the decision (a design_decisions entry: testament as the agent test runner, with the alternatives and the owner's date), then amend the Dev-commands row to name `testament run` and say whether a testament green counts as a green claim. Leave the prawduct `test_command` alone; it is the gate's runner.", "files": ["CLAUDE.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Test evidence missing at cumulative", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `prawduct-hook test-status` exits 1: there is no .test-evidence.json on disk. The change-log's 6636-passed pool run is prose, not evidence for this tree. Run the project's test_command (it uses `-n auto`, so it also exercises the per-process NUMBA_CACHE_DIR fix under xdist) before the PR.", "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "CLAUDE.md grows to 265 lines; the 87-line testament block is reference material", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The prior accept (R-16, 178 lines) was before this material change. This adds 87 lines of testament JSON-envelope reference to a file every song and engineering session loads, and the project's own norm keeps creative turns free of engineering framing. Move the block to a docs/ page, e.g. docs/testing-with-testament.md, and keep a 3-4 line pointer in CLAUDE.md: the run command, the exit-code meaning and the link. If testament must find its block verbatim in CLAUDE.md, record that constraint in the decision from the blocking finding.", "files": ["CLAUDE.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "The audio marker's help text still says the stack is unstable in containers, which the change-log says was corrected", "recommendation": "Scope: class. The conftest docstring and skip reason were corrected, but they have siblings. pyproject.toml:233's `audio` marker description (shown by `pytest --markers`) still reads \"set HALLUCINOTE_SKIP_AUDIO=1 to skip in CPU-only/container sessions where that stack is unstable.\" A maintainer reading it keeps skipping audio in containers and loses that coverage for no reason. The change-log's \"that note is corrected\" is false for this site. Search for `unstable` / `HALLUCINOTE_SKIP_AUDIO` across pyproject.toml, .github/workflows/ci.yml and docs/. Make the marker text relational, e.g. \"opt-out: HALLUCINOTE_SKIP_AUDIO=1\", and drop the instability claim.", "files": ["pyproject.toml"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "`.testament.toml` setup comment says \"same sync as CI\", but it syncs with `--frozen` where CI uses `--locked`", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. CI runs `uv sync --all-packages --all-extras --locked`, which fails on a stale lock. The setup step's `--frozen` installs whatever uv.lock says without checking it, so on a stale lock a pool run goes green where CI goes red. Either switch the setup step to `--locked` so it really matches CI, or delete \"same sync as CI\".", "files": [".testament.toml"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "Per-process numba cache dirs leak when a process dies abnormally", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. `atexit` does not run on SIGSEGV or SIGKILL, or on an xdist worker that is torn down hard, so each such process leaves a `numba-cache-*` dir (a full librosa JIT cache) in the temp dir. Pool containers are ephemeral and macOS ages out $TMPDIR, so the cost is small. If it matters locally, sweep stale `numba-cache-*` dirs older than a day at conftest import.", "files": ["conftest.py"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "learnings cross-check: the numba-segfault learning now names a superseded remedy for pytest runs", "recommendation": "Scope: none. In core.md, \"A segfaulting suite reports a SMALLER suite\" says to fix a numba crash by deleting site-packages `*.nbi`/`*.nbc`. Under pytest that cache is no longer read: each process gets its own NUMBA_CACHE_DIR. The deletion advice still applies to non-pytest consumers (the MCP server, scripts). When next touching learnings, say the pytest case is handled structurally by the root conftest. No other warned-against pattern recurs: the guard test plants its precondition, and the Dockerfile ps/procps addition traces to a real `ps` subprocess test.", "files": [".claude/rules/learnings/core.md"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "record-lint relay", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Two record-lint answers. (1) suite-total-claim at .prawduct/change-log.md:58 ('6636 passed'): append-only history, nothing reads it, no edit wanted. (2) learnings-core-raise-unapproved: project-state.yaml declares `learnings_budgets.core.md: 57KB` with no `owner_approved:` date, so the real cap is 12KB. This bundle did not touch project-state; only the owner can approve the raise. Raise it with the owner, or move rules to an area file.", "files": [".prawduct/change-log.md", ".prawduct/project-state.yaml"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "priors and backlog", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Priors: 21 matched. Only R-16 (CLAUDE.md size) is re-raised, because this bundle materially changed that file; the others are untouched. Backlog: cache searches for segfault, numba and container, plus `affecting conftest.py`, find no item this bundle resolves. No build plan claims this branch (scope unbound), so there are no plan goals to judge against. The work traces to the change-log entry's stated purpose (pool onboarding plus the crash it exposed), and every piece is consumed: the Dockerfile by .testament.toml, the conftest guard by every pytest process, the guard test by the suite.", "fid": "R-9"}], "counts": {"blocking": 1, "warning": 3, "note": 5}, "observations": [], "